sprint: 117.14
title: Sync, Backup & Conflict Validation
stage: RED
date: 2026-09-30
command: flutter test test/features/collaboration/application/conflict_resolver_test.dart
exit: 1
result: 5 pass / 2 fail (7 total after adding 2 regression tests)
failure_1: 'resolver keeps a remote-only edit instead of reverting it to base'
  expected: '2' (remote value)
  actual:   '1' (BASE value - the remote edit was reverted)
failure_2: 'resolver keeps a remote-only addition instead of dropping it'
  expected: {'b': '2'}
  actual:   {} (remote-only key vanished entirely)
root_cause: lib/features/collaboration/application/conflict_resolver.dart:27-31
  the merge only walks `change.ours.keys`. A key that only the remote side
  changed is not a conflict, so no resolution is supplied for it, and the key
  is simply never emitted. The merged state therefore either reverts a remote
  edit to the base value the user already replaced, or drops a remote-only
  addition without a trace. Both are silent loss of a synced edit, and
  117.14 declares 'conflicts' and 'restore' as required evidence.
pre_fix_sha256: 42d6c2984d92ff0db231bf89f326a1403382ac7c551a32eba9752a1fe3ed81ec
pre_fix_restored_via: git show HEAD:<path> (not git reset)
